                        "form": "лима́нами"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "2a5369a5-a316-49c6-870a-c12b43a01593",
                        "entry_id": "42bd10cf-511d-390b-afb1-acd682bb1cc1",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "лима́не"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "23967431-5d4c-43be-ac3e-91c2a8f6a0da",
                        "entry_id": "42bd10cf-511d-390b-afb1-acd682bb1cc1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "лима́нах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d4cb20e3-4d4e-38ef-98af-b55f05272519",
                        "entry_id": "42bd10cf-511d-390b-afb1-acd682bb1cc1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "геогр. залив в низовьях реки"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "41c1ed54-8d75-4e49-b890-7d4a718dafb9",
                                "sense_id": "d4cb20e3-4d4e-38ef-98af-b55f05272519",
                                "text": "Доплыв благополучно до лимана, они исправляли мачты, паруса, рули; входили в море и, держась западных берегов его, достигали Греции."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc7a1ef6-18d7-46a0-a7e8-6e61f4b01dde",
                                "sense_id": "d4cb20e3-4d4e-38ef-98af-b55f05272519",
                                "text": "Он послал шлюпки, которые из Охотского моря прошли в Амурский лиман, и таким образом оказалось, что Сахалин не соединен с материком, как прежде думали."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1e6ed8b9-b5e7-3f7b-93e9-cc33afd2be19",
                        "entry_id": "42bd10cf-511d-390b-afb1-acd682bb1cc1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "геогр. солёное озеро вблизи моря"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7075845-e8d4-4be5-977b-75b23bf3854e",
                                "sense_id": "1e6ed8b9-b5e7-3f7b-93e9-cc33afd2be19",
                                "text": "От Горького озера около осьми верст находится еще небольшое озерко, лиман называемое, которое в длину не более полуверсты, а в ширину около четверти версты занимает."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6cea69db-0f3a-4d7a-8bde-93a7cf5a45ff",
                                "sense_id": "1e6ed8b9-b5e7-3f7b-93e9-cc33afd2be19",
                                "text": "Только весной, после таяния снега, эти реки, мелкие понижения почвы и озёра-лиманы ненадолго заполняются водой, недостаточной для того, чтобы дать жизнь засушливым землям."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2a084104-2708-457f-b405-0788080c4009",
                        "source_entry_id": "42bd10cf-511d-390b-afb1-acd682bb1cc1",
                        "source_sense_description": "залив в низовьях реки",
                        "target_lang_word": "estuary",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "estuary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7799db3-3505-3d41-92df-9ef59aeeb04b",
                                        "entry_id": "1b6c6507-5169-3941-9fef-93e2f8c7ac00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A coastal water body where ocean tides and river water merge, resulting in a brackish water zone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45e853fe-03d1-4392-b840-48e3a456acbb",
                                                "sense_id": "d7799db3-3505-3d41-92df-9ef59aeeb04b",
                                                "text": "The railway then follows the widening estuary of the river, which at high tide has the appearance of a lake, but at low water presents a rather cheerless expanse of dark mud."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ffcc237-60e0-4e25-a6be-34accca0d7e0",
                                                "sense_id": "d7799db3-3505-3d41-92df-9ef59aeeb04b",
                                                "text": "There's something special about tidal estuaries, due to the abundance of wildlife and the ever-changing scenes as the water ebbs or rises. Throw in some moody skies and filtered sunlight, and the views can resemble a painting by Turner - only you don't have to go to the National Gallery to see this, it's brought to your seat on a train."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0e59965-2773-31b6-9c9f-7ae628450ee8",
                                        "entry_id": "1b6c6507-5169-3941-9fef-93e2f8c7ac00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ocean inlet also fed by fresh river water."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2d484519-2148-4bbe-ab66-52f0cfa19f90",
                        "source_entry_id": "42bd10cf-511d-390b-afb1-acd682bb1cc1",
                        "source_sense_description": "залив в низовьях реки",
                        "target_lang_word": "firth",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "firth",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3eb00ab-c3be-3112-b3a1-26afddeef99b",
                                        "entry_id": "251f7778-4a37-35ad-9677-41b72e67ec84",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An arm or inlet of the sea; a river estuary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2eb72210-311d-434d-91ca-8485fa3a636f",
                                                "sense_id": "d3eb00ab-c3be-3112-b3a1-26afddeef99b",
                                                "text": "The descent continues, still more steeply to Dundee (Tay Bridge), and approaching from the bridge itself this sharp descent gives the curious appearance that the station is below the level of the firth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4f8020a-3cad-443f-96ea-56b9cf1fb108",
                                                "sense_id": "d3eb00ab-c3be-3112-b3a1-26afddeef99b",
                                                "text": "They drove on, every rise in the road lifting their sightline clear of the drystone dykes along the roadside, gifting glimpses of the firth and the islands, the blue peaks of Arran."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "firth",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4520645e-73f7-38dc-9ab4-5c6db18c6ead",
                                        "entry_id": "4491e3d1-e3bc-36eb-beb0-da8b253111ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of frith (“a forest used for hunting; a (small) wood; wooded country; land covered mainly by brushwood”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Northern-England",
                                            "Scotland",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
